From: Majid Arasskhani <M.Arasskhani@gosilkroad.net>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 15:47:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/22] fix(providers): no resend of a paid POST after read
 timeout; explicit chat timeout; pool and duration ceilings configurable

Bug (B-16/B-17): post_openrouter_json retried on *any* transport error,
ReadTimeout and "server disconnected" included - the request body had
already reached OpenRouter, so the retry paid for the image or transcript a
second time. Image calls also carried three hard-coded 180 s timeouts next
to the IMAGE_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_SECONDS setting meant to control them, the
shared OpenRouter client was capped at 8 connections per worker (the ninth
concurrent request waited in PoolTimeout), the chat completion relied on
LiteLLM's implicit timeout, and VIDEO_MAX_DURATION_SECONDS existed in
config but was never applied.

Change:
- is_safe_to_resend_post(): only connect/write failures (body never left)
  are resent; read timeouts and post-send disconnects raise to the caller.
  The image strategy fallback loop (different strategy, spaced by
  OPENROUTER_EMPTY_IMAGE_RETRY_DELAYS_SEC) keeps its broader predicate on
  purpose - that is a documented product decision about Gemini drops.
- images.py uses image_request_timeout() everywhere (OPENROUTER_FALLBACK_
  TIMEOUT removed from its imports).
- OPENROUTER_MAX_CONNECTIONS (32) for the shared client pool.
- CHAT_PROVIDER_TIMEOUT_SECONDS (600) passed as timeout= to acompletion.
- videos.py enforces VIDEO_MAX_DURATION_SECONDS when set (400 above it).

Tests: tests/test_provider_timeouts.py; the two old tests that asserted
a resend after disconnect/read timeout now assert the new contract.

